---
// The splash figure: the tenant tree that the quick example on the same page
// creates. Keep the names, slugs and config key in step with that example, so
// the picture and the code teach one model.
---

<figure class="tenant-tree">
	<figcaption class="tenant-tree-label">Tenant hierarchy</figcaption>
	<ol class="tenant-tree-rows">
		<li class="tenant-row d0">
			<span class="tenant-depth">d0</span>
			<span class="tenant-name">AcmeSec</span>
			<span class="tenant-meta">root tenant</span>
		</li>
		<li class="tenant-row d1">
			<span class="tenant-depth">d1</span>
			<span class="tenant-name">NorthStar MSP</span>
			<span class="tenant-meta">child tenant</span>
		</li>
	</ol>
	<p class="tenant-config">
		<span class="tenant-config-key">max_users: <span class="tenant-config-value">1000</span></span>
		<span class="badge-inherited">inherited from d0</span>
	</p>
	<p class="tenant-tree-note">
		NorthStar MSP sets no value for <code>max_users</code>, so it resolves the value from its
		parent. The <a href="#quick-example">quick example</a> builds this tree.
	</p>
</figure>
